D069 (founder request, 2026-11-13; F6; wiki/decisions/D069-openai-ads-measurement.md): a paid order is reported to OpenAI
Ads (`order_created`) from the server as well as the browser. One import and one line in `notifyPaid`'s existing
`Promise.allSettled`: `reportOrderToOpenAi(order)` (src/lib/ads/openai-capi.ts, deliberately outside src/lib/store/). It
inherits the two guarantees the Meta and PostHog reports beside it rely on: it runs once per paid order, behind
`markPaid`'s atomic UPDATE, and it never throws. It makes no request without OPENAI_ADS_CAPI_KEY (a Vercel production
secret, read inside the function), off production, or for an order that carries no OpenAI click or browser reference.
`markPaid`, the refund, failure and not-payable paths, the emails and every other line of this file are unchanged.

D074 (founder sign-off, chat 26 Nov 2026; K-124; wiki/decisions/D074-refund-event.md): a refund the webhook applies is
reported to PostHog (`purchase_refunded`) from the server, beside the sale it undoes. The D069 paragraph above leaves the
refund path alone; D074 changes it, and only as follows. In `markRefunded`: the existing import line also takes
`reportRefundToPostHog` (src/lib/store/posthog-server.ts, itself under a reviewed patch); the order SELECT also reads
`tier, utm, ph_distinct_id`; and an `await reportRefund(...)` follows the full-refund UPDATE and the partial branch's log
line. `reportRefund` is a small local function whose try/catch is the never-throw rule (the frozen fulfil.test.ts mocks
./posthog-server without the new export, and its three markRefunded tests must stay green). `markRefunded`'s return
values and its status update, the webhook route, `markPaid`, `notifyPaid`, the emails and every other line of this file
are unchanged. Nothing goes to Meta, GA4 or OpenAI, and no name, phone, email, address, child age, payment id or refund id
is sent.

